hey guys it's max from axe sect today we  are getting our first hands-on  impression with the Google pixel for of  course this phone has been leaked like  crazy Google announced it already I  think this is the case but we just got  it in thanks to Google part of the pixel  program so thank you guys for sending  that out of course we're gonna be doing  our standard comparisons we're gonna  have a great photo comparison maybe some  astrophotography stuff so you guys  definitely don't want to miss out on  those but for now we can only do  hands-on unboxing impressions so let's  do it now I didn't know which color  we're gonna get so it looks like we got  the white one I think let's pull this  out and I'll just give you guys kind of  an impression using this phone and how  it feels like in the hand all those kind  of things that you can't really get from  the spec sheet because obviously you  guys already know all of the specs so  first impressions it feels kind of slim  but I don't know let's see let's get  this one out my this is my 11 Pro max  and yeah you guys might be able to tell  that the pixel 4 is slightly slimmer on  the sides then my 11 Pro max now the  other thing that I'm noticing is that  this little plastic little insert  between the glass and the display it's  not as smooth as it is on iPhone I  thought it's almost seamless you don't  notice it here it sticks out kind of  like I had iPhone 6 where I put in an  aftermarket display and it didn't sit  flush so that's instantly noticeable  it's also slightly taller than my 11 Pro  max that's interesting not by much but  you do notice it now on the back the  finish is much smoother so even though  this is a matte finish it is almost like  it's glossy just slightly matte compared  to this thing it's a very I don't know  how to describe a sandy feeling it feels  a lot more like satin compared to the  matte glass back of the iPhone now  another interesting thing that I wasn't  expecting is how grippy these sides are  so we have this matte black frame  aluminum frame but I expect it to be  very slippery like the iPhone ones but  it's almost like it has a little bit of  a texture and it feels quite nice I  would have to say that this phone feels  nicer in the hand  more confidence holding it compared to  holding my iPhone 11 Pro max now I have  this set up here for face unlock and a  lot of things that Google is doing here  just reminds me of what Apple is doing I  don't know if I'm allowed to say that  but it is what it is so I absolutely  love face unlock Hey it's actually  telling me where to go  all right well this is more difficult  than on the iPhone hold the phone steady  rotate your head  go slow okay oh there we go I guess it  was working that's it not a second time  like the iPhones do interesting all  right let's continue of course we have  the navigation that is similar to the  iPhone now with the latest version of  Android which I do like so we have the  face unlock just like on the iPhones I  love that we have the navigation swipe  up go side to side I love that let's  flip it around and take a look at our  cameras over here so as you guys can  tell this looks very similar to the  renders of the iPhone before they did  the all glass back I think the fact that  they added the dark frame the black  frame on the sides makes this complete  back camera array look much better than  if they would have had this and had like  a silver edge or a white edge or color  matched it but I don't think it looks as  nice as something like that now we do  have the little power button that is a  little offset on the color I'm not a big  fan of that but it is what it is let's  test out the new radar feature and one  thing that's really cool I think  probably the coolest thing is when you  reach out for the phone you actually see  that little lock icon that pops up so it  knows that you're going for your phone  so Prime's the whole array of sensors  that are hidden right up here inside  this forehead that way as soon as you  pick up your phone BAM it doesn't locks  that is that is really quick so not only  do we have as you guys can see this  always-on display  it actually unlocks for you  automatically and I really like that of  course with the iPhone we do not have  all of our little notifications at the  top of this little bar you have to see  it at the home screen or the lock screen  unless it's hidden away so with the  iPhone they have to have force you to  you know turn on the phone and then  swipe up to get in there whereas with  this you have the advantage of just  speed bam you're right there and you can  start doing whatever you want to do now  just like with the face unlock that I  love with other device we also have our  new gesture based navigation now this is  something I complained about with the  pixel 3 with the new software they added  this and I love being able to go back  quickly much quicker and much more  efficient and a swipe up to get to your  home screen now one thing I'm really  curious about is the sound quality we no  longer have those dual front firing  speakers we still have a stereo setup  but let's go ahead and see how good it  sounds because I was always a strong  suit of the pixel  [Music]  interesting very interesting so I hear a  lot of separation inside of it sounding  like the sound is coming from the phone  I feel like I hear the right channel  separate from the left channel it's not  blending in definitely isn't super loud  but first impressions not bad the  clarity is definitely there  now Google sent us the Excel version and  this thing has a really high res display  and they really were talking about how  great the display is the contrast ratio  though is not as high as some others and  I maxed out the brightness right now and  it's not blindingly bright now it may  get brighter in auto brightness modes  we'll have to check that later for our  full review but here it's pretty good  when we max it out and now let's go  ahead and open up a YouTube video and  man I really like the the little  navigation at the bottom works so well  and this is and it's an 8k HDR video of  course we can't playback an 8k but  thankfully we can playback in 1440p 60  with HDR and so that actually matches  the panel and here I mean the image  looks really good  Wow really good colors the HDR is  looking good and as far as detail and  sharpness and brightness watching this  HDR video it looks quite good now  something I'm noticing is that the  little the way that display is rounded  it is quite substantial here in the  corners it kind of stands out a little  bit and especially having that forehead  be offset with the chin that gives it a  little bit of a weird look compared to a  lot of other phones but the quality  looks nice now one interesting thing is  the choice of having a telephoto instead  of an ultra wide I personally use the  telephoto more although I think it is  more important to have an ultra wide of  course we have a lot of other things to  take a look at one thing I'm very  curious about is the battery life  because we have this 90 Hertz display  which is part of the reason why I just  felt so fluid while I was testing this  and these new gestures we'll see how  that will be affecting the 3800 milliamp  hour battery we do have a decent charger  18y USB type-c that looks surprisingly  familiar  here so that's something we're going to  be testing out of course we're going to  do ass wide variety of comparisons  looking at all the different aspects and  some detailed photo comparisons that you  guys have seen in the past so make sure  you guys are subscribed if you guys have  any questions ask in the comment section  below we'll try to adjust those in our  full review that we're going to be  working on thank you guys for watching  that has been max and I will see you in  the next video  [Music]

